    "['binding tunnel [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel gre\\n##\\n\\nThe `binding tunnel gre` command in Huawei associates the physical interface with a GRE tunnel. In Juniper, this is achieved by configuring the interface with `family inet tunnel gre` under the interface configuration. The IP address configuration is also included as it's part of the original interface configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel gre', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.2.10/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel gre\\n##\\n\\nThe `binding tunnel gre` command in Huawei associates the physical interface with a GRE tunnel. In Juniper, this is achieved by configuring the interface with `family inet tunnel gre` under the interface configuration. The IP address configuration is also included as it's part of the original interface configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel gre'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel protection ipsec profile [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gt-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel ipsec-vpn profile IPSEC-PROFILE', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces gt-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel ipsec-vpn profile IPSEC-PROFILE\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n1. \"gt-0/0/0\" represents the GRE tunnel interface (equivalent to Tunnel0 in Huawei)\\n2. The \"unit 0\" is required as Juniper uses logical units for interface configuration\\n3. \"ipsec-vpn profile\" is Juniper\\'s equivalent syntax for tunnel protection with an IPSec profile', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gt-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel ipsec-vpn profile IPSEC-PROFILE'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel-protocol [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI `tunnel-protocol gre p2mp` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Juniper, GRE tunnels are typically configured under `gr` (GRE) interfaces rather than generic tunnel interfaces.\\n2. The `multipoint` parameter is Juniper's equivalent to HUAWEI's `p2mp` (point-to-multipoint) designation.\\n3. The interface name (`gr-0/0/0`) would need to match your specific Juniper device's available interface.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI `tunnel-protocol gre p2mp` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel encapsulation gre\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Juniper, GRE tunnels are typically configured under `gr` (GRE) interfaces rather than generic tunnel interfaces.\\n2. The `multipoint` parameter is Juniper's equivalent to HUAWEI's `p2mp` (point-to-multipoint) designation.\\n3. The interface name (`gr-0/0/0`) would need to match your specific Juniper device's available interface.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel multipoint'}]]": 1,
    "['source [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source interface ge-1/0/0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source interface ge-1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, GRE tunnels are configured under `gr-0/0/0` (GR = GRE interface)\\n2. The `unit 0` specifies the logical unit, similar to the interface instance in Huawei\\n3. `tunnel source interface` is the Juniper equivalent to Huawei's `source` command for tunnel configuration\\n4. `ge-1/0/0` is Juniper's interface naming for GigabitEthernet1/0/0 (ge = Gigabit Ethernet)\\n\\nNote: The actual interface name might vary slightly based on Juniper platform (e.g., it could be `ge-1/0/0.0` if using a specific unit). The translation maintains the same logical function of setting the tunnel's source interface.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source interface ge-1/0/0'}]]": 1,
