    "['nhrp entry [parameter1] [parameter2] register', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols nhrp interface tun.0 shortcut', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI NHRP registration command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 shortcut\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 registry-holdtime 300\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 record 172.16.1.1/32 nhs 10.1.1.10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. `shortcut` enables NHRP shortcut switching (equivalent to HUAWEI's `nhrp shortcut`)\\n2. `registry-holdtime` sets the registration timeout (default 300 seconds)\\n3. The `record` command creates the NHS entry mapping the hub's tunnel IP (172.16.1.1) to its physical IP (10.1.1.10)\\n\\nNote: Juniper requires the tunnel interface to be specified (here as tun.0 - adjust according to your actual interface name) and uses a slightly different syntax structure than HUAWEI's single-line command.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols nhrp interface tun.0 shortcut'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols nhrp interface tun.0 registry-holdtime 300', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI NHRP registration command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 shortcut\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 registry-holdtime 300\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 record 172.16.1.1/32 nhs 10.1.1.10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. `shortcut` enables NHRP shortcut switching (equivalent to HUAWEI's `nhrp shortcut`)\\n2. `registry-holdtime` sets the registration timeout (default 300 seconds)\\n3. The `record` command creates the NHS entry mapping the hub's tunnel IP (172.16.1.1) to its physical IP (10.1.1.10)\\n\\nNote: Juniper requires the tunnel interface to be specified (here as tun.0 - adjust according to your actual interface name) and uses a slightly different syntax structure than HUAWEI's single-line command.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols nhrp interface tun.0 registry-holdtime 300'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols nhrp interface tun.0 record 172.16.1.1/32 nhs 10.1.1.10', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI NHRP registration command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 shortcut\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 registry-holdtime 300\\nset protocols nhrp interface tun.0 record 172.16.1.1/32 nhs 10.1.1.10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. `shortcut` enables NHRP shortcut switching (equivalent to HUAWEI's `nhrp shortcut`)\\n2. `registry-holdtime` sets the registration timeout (default 300 seconds)\\n3. The `record` command creates the NHS entry mapping the hub's tunnel IP (172.16.1.1) to its physical IP (10.1.1.10)\\n\\nNote: Juniper requires the tunnel interface to be specified (here as tun.0 - adjust according to your actual interface name) and uses a slightly different syntax structure than HUAWEI's single-line command.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols nhrp interface tun.0 record 172.16.1.1/32 nhs 10.1.1.10'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel protection ipsec profile [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set security ipsec vpn IPSEC-PROFILE bind-interface st0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI \"tunnel protection ipsec profile\" statement:\\n\\n##\\nset security ipsec vpn IPSEC-PROFILE bind-interface st0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Juniper, IPsec profiles are typically configured under the `security ipsec` hierarchy\\n2. The interface binding is done with `bind-interface` parameter\\n3. Juniper commonly uses st0 interfaces for tunnels (similar to GRE tunnels)\\n4. The actual interface name (st0.0 in this example) would need to match your Juniper tunnel interface configuration\\n5. This assumes you\\'ve already configured the IPsec profile named \"IPSEC-PROFILE\" in the Juniper configuration', 'trans_template': 'set security ipsec vpn IPSEC-PROFILE bind-interface st0.0'}]]": 1,
